In that test (the §17 one in `packages/core/test/cache.test.ts` — it's actually the *adjacent* test to the byte-identical/second-submission one; the `bytes` object lives in "records the injected tokenizer id on every outcome so swapping tokenizers is a deliberate diff rather than a silent shift of every recorded range"), the simulator is constructed with a custom tokenizer:

```ts
const bytes = new ProviderCacheSimulator({
  tokenizer: new ExactTokenizer('bytes-v0', (text) => text.length),
}).submit(prompt);
